WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.221
Convolutional graph networks have two weaknesses.

00:00:03.301 --> 00:00:06.589
Because their filters come from graph polynomials,

00:00:06.669 --> 00:00:10.159
they lack expressiveness on a small parameter budget.

00:00:10.239 --> 00:00:14.403
And they cannot learn hierarchical, multi-scale
features alone,

00:00:14.483 --> 00:00:18.175
needing bolt-on tricks like clustering or node dropping.

00:00:18.255 --> 00:00:25.315
Image CNNs have neither problem: local learning and
shared filters naturally capture multi-scale patterns.

00:00:25.395 --> 00:00:29.020
But their Euclidean convolution assumes a regular grid,

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:31.310
and does not fit irregular graphs.
